ASSUMPTIONS:
- Each source date is reduced to its date part by taking the text before any "T" (time of day ignored).
- Partial dates: year-month becomes day 1; year-only becomes 1 January. Any other text (not matching YYYY, YYYY-MM or YYYY-MM-DD) is treated as unusable and skipped.
- Impossible calendar dates (e.g. 2014-02-30) are treated as unusable and skipped.
- AE, lab and TRTEDT records are matched to subjects by USUBJID only; records for USUBJIDs not in DM are ignored.
- LSTALVDT is the maximum over all usable dates from AESTDTC, AEENDTC, LBDTC and TRTEDT, with no separate handling of death dates (DTHDTC is not in the spec).
- All DM subjects are output, including those with no usable date (LSTALVDT null), with one row per USUBJID.
- none of these choices would change the output in a way the spec leaves open, so no escalation is needed.

